89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (The Coupon & Discount Manager is a console-based application that manages discount coupons with unique codes, validity dates and usage limits. It is a beginner-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project built with Java.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (A Binary Search Tree \(BST\) organizes the coupons by code so that they can be stored and listed in sorted order. A HashMap stores the same coupons against their codes, which allows direct lookup of any coupon in constant time on average. A greedy strategy compares all valid coupons for a given bill and chooses the one that gives the highest saving. Sorting is used to produce coupon reports, and file handling is used to load coupon data from coupons.txt at start-up and save the usage updates when the program exits.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Before a coupon is applied, the program checks that the coupon exists, that the current date lies within its validity range, that its usage limit has not been reached and that the discount never exceeds the bill amount. The project uses a small text file instead of a database, which keeps the scope suitable for a college-level submission.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
92 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 61 0 R
/T (Introduction)
/E (Introduction)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Discount coupons are a common feature of shopping websites, restaurants, billing counters and mobile payment apps. A good coupon system must find the coupon quickly, check whether it can still be used and make sure the customer receives the best possible saving without the discount becoming larger than the bill.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (This project demonstrates the idea on a small scale. The user adds coupons with a code, a discount type \(percentage or flat amount\), a discount value, a start date, an end date and a usage limit. When a bill is entered, the program looks up the coupon code using the HashMap, validates it, calculates the discount and prints the final bill. If no code is given, the greedy strategy checks every valid coupon and applies the best one. Coupon reports are printed in sorted order, and all changes are saved to a file.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
